# LabscriptAI OT

Use the bundled `opentrons-lab` MCP server and `skills/opentrons-*` skills for Opentrons protocol authoring, simulation, and safe runtime checks.

For new experiments, start with `opentrons-experiment-run`. Setup: [docs/GETTING_STARTED.md](../../docs/GETTING_STARTED.md).

Before new protocol authoring, read robot_authoring_context() locally and use the saved authoring_context; reuse across chats/restarts even when the robot is offline. Capture once or explicitly refresh with robot_authoring_context(refresh=true) when online. Missing snapshots can use supplied hardware constraints without requiring a connection. Explicit offline/local-only/no-connection requests never refresh over the network. Refresh live state before execution. Follow policy/workflows.md.

Live robot motion is opt-in. Run simulation before unattended live execution. Treat vision as observation-only. After authoring and simulation, refresh the dashboard before optional deck vision → optional liquid probe → execution. Honor explicit scoped software-check waivers per policy/safety-policy.md; the probe opt-in flag gates probe motion only.
